On 1st April 2019 two new unitary authorities (UAs) and three new district councils (DCs) were formed. Figures are no longer collected on the previous geographic basis.
Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole UA from Bournemouth UA, Poole UA and Christchurch district council;
Dorset UA from East Dorset, North Dorset, West Dorset, Purbeck, Weymouth and Portland district councils;
East Suffolk district council from Suffolk Coastal and Waveney district councils;
West Suffolk district council from Forest Heath and St. Edmundsbury district councils;
Somerset West and Taunton district council from Taunton Deane and West Somerset district councils.

On 1st April 2021 two new unitary authorities (UAs) were formed. Figures are no longer collected on the previous geographic basis.
North Northamptonshire UA from Corby, East Northamptonshire, Kettering and Wellingborough district councils;
West Northamptonshire UA from Northampton, Daventry, and South Northamptonshire district councils.
